  user_input {
    user_response: "\n**Role:** Expert Frontend Architect (Next.js App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS).\n\n**Project Context:**\nYou are building the UI components for \"DealPlate,\" a mobile-first web application for university students in Nairobi. The UI must reflect a premium, high-energy \"Flash Deal\" aesthetic called \"High-Velocity Appetite.\"\n\n**Task:**\nWrite production-ready Next.js components and pages based on the images I have uploaded. **Do not hallucinate the file structure; generate the code based strictly on the following coding conventions and design system tokens.** **1. Tailwind Color Palette Enforcement:**\n\n* **Primary Actions & Highlights:** Strictly use `#FF6B00` (`bg-[#FF6B00]`, `text-[#FF6B00]`).\n* **Urgency / Flash Alerts / Badges:** Strictly use `#E11D48` (`bg-[#E11D48]`, `text-[#E11D48]`).\n* **Surface & Backgrounds:** Use `#F3F4F6` for subtle card backgrounds and `#FFFFFF` for the main canvas.\n* **Text & Neutrals:** Use `#111827` for high-contrast primary text and `#5a4136` or `#8e7164` for subtle secondary text.\n\n**2. Typography Rules:**\n\n* **Headers & Prices:** Map to `Plus Jakarta Sans`. Use Tailwind classes like `font-bold tracking-tight` for headlines.\n* **Body & Labels:** Map to `Inter`. Use `text-base leading-relaxed` for readability.\n* **Currency Convention:** Every price must include \"Ksh\" formatted explicitly (e.g., `<span className=\"text-sm\">Ksh</span> <span className=\"text-2xl font-bold\">600</span>`).\n\n**3. Component & Shape Architecture:**\n\n* **Buttons:** Must have a minimum touch target of 48px (`h-12` or `min-h-[48px]`), use `rounded-lg` (16px), and include tactile feedback (`active:scale-95 transition-transform`).\n* **Badges & Tags:** Must use `rounded-full` (pill-shaped), bold text, and small sizing (`text-xs font-bold px-3 py-1`).\n* **Deal Cards:** Must use `rounded-lg`, a `shadow-sm` for depth, and an `aspect-video` (16:9) container for the top image. Discount badges must be `absolute` positioned over the top-left of the image.\n* **Inputs:** Clean 1px border (`border-[#F3F4F6]`). On focus, transition to `focus:ring-2 focus:ring-[#FF6B00] outline-none`.\n\n**4. Layout & Spacing Engine:**\n\n* **Grid:** Adhere to an 8-point grid layout (use standard Tailwind spacing like `p-4`, `gap-2`, `mt-6`).\n* **Responsiveness:** Build mobile-first. Use a single column by default, shifting to a 2-column grid (`sm:grid-cols-2`) on tablets, capped at a maximum width of 1200px (`max-w-7xl mx-auto`) for desktop screens.\n* **Margins:** Maintain consistent 16px (`px-4`) horizontal padding on mobile containers.\n\n**5. State & Data Simulation:**\n\n* **Mock Data:** Define a strict TypeScript interface for `Deal`. Populate it with highly realistic, appetizing placeholder data suitable for Nairobi university students. Do not use generic \"Lorem Ipsum\".\n* **Interactions:** For the checkout flow, implement a simulated M-Pesa Daraja payment state using React `useState` and `setTimeout` to mimic network latency before showing a success state.\n\n**Execution:** Look at the uploaded screenshots and generate the corresponding Next.js code adhering perfectly to these conventions. Output the complete code blocks without truncating."
    items {
      text: "\n**Role:** Expert Frontend Architect (Next.js App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS).\n\n**Project Context:**\nYou are building the UI components for \"DealPlate,\" a mobile-first web application for university students in Nairobi. The UI must reflect a premium, high-energy \"Flash Deal\" aesthetic called \"High-Velocity Appetite.\"\n\n**Task:**\nWrite production-ready Next.js components and pages based on the images I have uploaded. **Do not hallucinate the file structure; generate the code based strictly on the following coding conventions and design system tokens.** **1. Tailwind Color Palette Enforcement:**\n\n* **Primary Actions & Highlights:** Strictly use `#FF6B00` (`bg-[#FF6B00]`, `text-[#FF6B00]`).\n* **Urgency / Flash Alerts / Badges:** Strictly use `#E11D48` (`bg-[#E11D48]`, `text-[#E11D48]`).\n* **Surface & Backgrounds:** Use `#F3F4F6` for subtle card backgrounds and `#FFFFFF` for the main canvas.\n* **Text & Neutrals:** Use `#111827` for high-contrast primary text and `#5a4136` or `#8e7164` for subtle secondary text.\n\n**2. Typography Rules:**\n\n* **Headers & Prices:** Map to `Plus Jakarta Sans`. Use Tailwind classes like `font-bold tracking-tight` for headlines.\n* **Body & Labels:** Map to `Inter`. Use `text-base leading-relaxed` for readability.\n* **Currency Convention:** Every price must include \"Ksh\" formatted explicitly (e.g., `<span className=\"text-sm\">Ksh</span> <span className=\"text-2xl font-bold\">600</span>`).\n\n**3. Component & Shape Architecture:**\n\n* **Buttons:** Must have a minimum touch target of 48px (`h-12` or `min-h-[48px]`), use `rounded-lg` (16px), and include tactile feedback (`active:scale-95 transition-transform`).\n* **Badges & Tags:** Must use `rounded-full` (pill-shaped), bold text, and small sizing (`text-xs font-bold px-3 py-1`).\n* **Deal Cards:** Must use `rounded-lg`, a `shadow-sm` for depth, and an `aspect-video` (16:9) container for the top image. Discount badges must be `absolute` positioned over the top-left of the image.\n* **Inputs:** Clean 1px border (`border-[#F3F4F6]`). On focus, transition to `focus:ring-2 focus:ring-[#FF6B00] outline-none`.\n\n**4. Layout & Spacing Engine:**\n\n* **Grid:** Adhere to an 8-point grid layout (use standard Tailwind spacing like `p-4`, `gap-2`, `mt-6`).\n* **Responsiveness:** Build mobile-first. Use a single column by default, shifting to a 2-column grid (`sm:grid-cols-2`) on tablets, capped at a maximum width of 1200px (`max-w-7xl mx-auto`) for desktop screens.\n* **Margins:** Maintain consistent 16px (`px-4`) horizontal padding on mobile containers.\n\n**5. State & Data Simulation:**\n\n* **Mock Data:** Define a strict TypeScript interface for `Deal`. Populate it with highly realistic, appetizing placeholder data suitable for Nairobi university students. Do not use generic \"Lorem Ipsum\".\n* **Interactions:** For the checkout flow, implement a simulated M-Pesa Daraja payment state using React `useState` and `setTimeout` to mimic network latency before showing a success state.\n\n**Execution:** Look at the uploaded screenshots and generate the corresponding Next.js code adhering perfectly to these conventions. Output the complete code blocks without truncating."
    }
